    \"t\",\r\n    metadata,\r\n    sa.Column(\"id\", sa.Integer, primary_key=True),\r\n    sa.Column(\"data\", sa.String(20)),\r\n)\r\n\r\ne = sa.create_engine(\r\n    \"postgresql+psycopg2://scott:tiger@127.0.0.1:5432/test\"  # , echo=True\r\n)\r\nwith e.connect() as c:\r\n    metadata.create_all(c)\r\n\r\n    r = c.execute(\r\n        t.insert().returning(t.c.data, sort_by_parameter_order=True),\r\n        [{\"data\": \"a\"}, {\"data\": \"b\"}],\r\n    )\r\n    print(r.all())\r\n    r = c.execute(\r\n        t.insert().returning(t.c.data, sort_by_parameter_order=True),\r\n        [{\"data\": \"a\"}, {\"data\": \"b\"}],\r\n    )\r\n    print(r.unique().all())\r\n```\r\nthe above prints\r\n```\r\n[('a',), ('b',)]\r\n[('a', 3), ('b', 4)]\r\n```\r\nwhile it should print `[('a',), ('b',)]` twice.\r\n\r\nThe issue is likely that `CursorResult` does not set `sentinel_filter` as the tuple filter of the metadata","closed_by":{"login":"sqlalchemy-bot","id":36047385,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MDQ3Mzg1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36047385?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/sqlalchemy-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sqlalchemy-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/sqlalchemy/sq